# .hmaignore — opena2a HackMyAgent self-scan scope exclusions.
#
# Exactly two single-file rules, each a triaged false positive on dev-only
# code outside the published npm `files` set (`dist`, `README.md`). Every
# rule must be a single existing file, preceded by comment lines naming the
# check id and a public issue; packages/cli/__tests__/hmaignore-scope.test.ts
# enforces that shape and refuses additions, negations, directory rules, and
# anything under packages/cli/src/. Fix real findings in source instead.

# NEMO-007 (full process.env passthrough to subprocess): dev-only lock-trace
# instrument, not published. Its measured purpose is spawning this repo's own
# vitest in the full inherited environment to reproduce lock contention;
# narrowing the env spread would change what the instrument measures.
# Triaged as a false positive: github.com/opena2a-org/opena2a/issues/188
packages/cli/scripts/shield-lock-trace-loop.ts

# NEMO-008 (TOCTOU race between verify and apply): the matcher pairs an
# integrity-check token in this test file's dynamic import with a spawn()
# in the unrelated concurrent-write test. No artifact is verified and then
# executed anywhere on that path; the two files share no artifact at all.
# Triaged as a false positive: github.com/opena2a-org/opena2a/issues/188
packages/cli/__tests__/shield/events.test.ts
